drm/amd/display: genlock Apple iMac 5K dual-tile panels (deterministic)

The internal panel on the 27" 5K iMacs (iMac15,1 / 17,1 / 18,3 / 19,1 /
iMacPro1,1 / 20,x) is a 2x1 tiled display: two 2560x2880 halves driven
over two separate links (eDP root + a second DP tile), combined into one
5120x2880 image. Once both tiles are woken/trained, the panel's TCON only
latches native dual-tile mode when the two tile streams scan out in
lockstep; otherwise the image is black (endless re-modeset) or, once up,
the seam shears.

dm_enable_per_frame_crtc_master_sync() sets up each stream's event_source
(master) but never enables the per-frame CRTC reset -- the
multi_sync_enabled path is a standing TODO ("read AMD VSDB bits ... for
now it's set to false"). triggered_crtc_reset.enabled stays false,
enable_timing_multisync() finds nothing to program and the tiles free-run.

A first version of this fix enabled the reset on the non-master stream
after set_master_stream(). That turned out to be a coin flip per modeset:
set_master_stream() only considers streams whose reset is ALREADY enabled
and falls back to stream[0], so the outcome depended on a stale flag
surviving from the previous commit. Measured on an iMac18,3 over seven
modesets: every commit where both tile streams carried the reset locked;
every one where only one did sheared -- at any bit depth.

So enable the reset on both tile streams (link->tiled_peer, wired by the
Apple panel quirk) BEFORE the master pick. The pick is then deterministic
and both tiles are in the hardware sync group; enable_timing_multisync()
programs the GSL per-frame position reset on DCE
(dce110_enable_per_frame_crtc_position_reset) and the panel presents a
stable, seamless 5120x2880 image. Verified 6/6 modesets locked, including
the clean boot commit where no stale flag could help.

Tested on an iMac18,3 (Radeon Pro 575, POLARIS10, DCE 11.2). Applies to
any tree that carries the tile-pair wiring (tiled_peer); the same hunk is
folded into imac5k-lean-core-7.2.x.patch.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ dm_enable_per_frame_crtc_master_sync(struct dc_state *context)
 		 * For now it's set to false
 		 */
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Apple iMac 5K dual-tile panel: the two tile streams must scan out
+	 * in lockstep or the panel TCON never latches dual-tile mode (black
+	 * screen / endless re-modeset) and, once up, the seam shears.
+	 * Mainline leaves per-frame CRTC master sync disabled (the
+	 * multi_sync_enabled TODO above). set_master_stream() only considers
+	 * streams whose reset is already enabled and falls back to stream[0],
+	 * so enabling the reset after the pick made the outcome depend on a
+	 * stale flag surviving from the previous commit: measured on an
+	 * iMac18,3, every commit where both tile streams carried the reset
+	 * locked, every one where only one did sheared. Flag both tiles up
+	 * front so the pick is deterministic and both are in the sync group.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < context->stream_count; i++) {
+		stream = context->streams[i];
+		if (stream && stream->link && stream->link->tiled_peer)
+			stream->triggered_crtc_reset.enabled = true;
+	}
+
 	set_master_stream(context->streams, context->stream_count);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < context->stream_count ; i++) {
